    "notes": "The PMTiles footprint and four open courtyards determine the model’s local frame. Each court has a separate tier and the hillside remains visible around it. The model reconstructs the upper fort and four principal palace courts within the mapped footprint. Maota Lake, Kesar Kyari, approach paths, dispersed hill walls and independent neighboring buildings use the host map. The standard six-meter terrain grid smooths retaining-wall faces and the grade below the zigzag approaches. The authored court decks follow the stepped layout and retain the surrounding terrain. The carved screens and painted ornament read at World Viewer scale. Tunnels and mirrored interiors are outside this exterior reconstruction."
  },
